corbell5571@juno.com (Corbell5571) writes:
> My 10th lvl gnome wizard turned herself into a vampire. Armor class
> and strength greatly improved, but hit points actually decreased. Will
> she ever become an 11 HD vampire (and correspondingly better wizard),
> or must she transform back into gnome for that to happen?

Experience points and levels gained (or drained) while polyselfed
accrue to your underlying form, and when you revert, you'll do so into
a stronger (or weaker) whatever-you-were. The displayed hit dice of
your monster form won't change while you're in it (it's just the base
for that monster type), but each level you gain will increase your HP
and max HP in your monster form by d8; losing levels _won't_ decrease
max HP.

